From e362e98a1f5a0c299b26e5d32bd249ea52be5cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:52:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Add owner moderation: block, lock, kick +
 blocked-by-owner page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the admin Live view, each user row now has Block / Lock / Kick
controls (with an optional message to show the user).

Worker:
- mod:<user> state in KV (active | blocked | locked + kickNonce + reason).
- POST /admin/moderate (token-gated) sets it; GET /status?user= is a
  read-only poll for clients; /track returns the caller's state on every
  beat; /admin/summary stamps each user with their state.
- The /v1 OpenAI proxy checks the caller's X-GPA-User against the block
  list and returns 403 blocked_by_owner — the one piece of enforcement a
  user can't edit out of their own browser.

Client:
- Polls /status every 15s (and reads it off each heartbeat). Blocked ->
  full-screen "Blocked by the owner" overlay + local AI cut-off (so
  Gemini, which bypasses the worker, is stopped too). Locked -> lighter
  freeze overlay. Kick (nonce bump past this session's baseline) -> forced
  sign-out with a message. Sends X-GPA-User on proxy calls.
- explainError surfaces the block reason instead of a generic message.

The honest limits are documented in the README and the panel: client-side
controls can be edited out by a determined user; the server-side proxy
gate is the real tooth, but can't cover Gemini or direct-mode/own-key use.

Tested: worker moderation against a mock KV (state set/read, token gate,
proxy 403 for blocked + pass-through for others, kick nonce, track/summary
state) and the client in Chromium (block shows the page with reason and
refuses AI, unblock clears it, kick signs out).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019GqTQm8E1znRkM37YVj6K7
